## Environment

- `iverilog` (Icarus Verilog 12) and `vvp` are pre-installed
- `python3` is available

## How to Run Tests

The test framework uses source and sink `.vmh` (Verilog Memory Hex) files.
Each testbench is compiled with `iverilog`, then run with `vvp` passing
`+test_cases_path=<dir>/` and `+test_case=<stem>` plusargs.

### Run all 18 tests (runs the verifier):

```bash
bash /tests/test.sh
```

### Run a specific testbench manually:

```bash
PITON=/app/piton
INFR=$PITON/verif/env/test_infrstrct

# Compile
iverilog -g2001 \
  -I "$INFR" \
  $PITON/design/chip/tile/sparc/ifu/rtl/sparc_ifu_esl_counter.v \
  $INFR/test_source.v $INFR/test_sink.v $INFR/test_infrstrct_fifo.v \
  $PITON/verif/env/ifu_esl_counter/ifu_esl_counter_top.v \
  -o /tmp/counter_sim.vvp

# Run one test case
vvp /tmp/counter_sim.vvp \
  +test_cases_path=$PITON/verif/env/ifu_esl_counter/test_cases/ \
  +test_case=test_step
```

A passing test prints something like `Simulation -> PASS (HIT GOOD TRAP)`.
A failing test prints `[FAILED]` or `Simulation -> FAIL (HIT BAD TRAP)`.

### Counter test cases (8):
`test_clear`, `test_clear_set`, `test_pause`, `test_set`,
`test_step`, `test_step_clear`, `test_step_clear_set`, `test_step_set`

### LFSR test cases (5):
`test_exhaust`, `test_ldstep`, `test_pause`, `test_seed`, `test_state0`

### Shiftreg test cases (4):
`test_pause`, `test_set`, `test_set_shift`, `test_shift`

### UART serializer test cases (1):
`test`

## Understanding the Modules

### sparc_ifu_esl_counter

Found in `piton/design/chip/tile/sparc/ifu/rtl/sparc_ifu_esl_counter.v`.
The `.core` file shows:
- Parameterized `COUNT_BIT_WIDTH` (default 16)
- Inputs: `clk`, `rst_n`, `step`, `clear`, `set`
- Output: `count_f [COUNT_BIT_WIDTH-1:0]`
- Priority: `clear` > `set` > `step`

### sparc_ifu_esl_lfsr

Found in `piton/design/chip/tile/sparc/ifu/rtl/sparc_ifu_esl_lfsr.v`.
- 16-bit LFSR, polynomial x^16 + x^14 + x^13 + x^11 + 1
- Inputs: `clk`, `rst_n`, `lfsr_seed[15:0]`, `lfsr_ld`, `lfsr_step`
- Outputs: `lfsr_state_f[15:0]`, `lfsr_out_f` (MSB of state)

### sparc_ifu_esl_shiftreg

Found in `piton/design/chip/tile/sparc/ifu/rtl/sparc_ifu_esl_shiftreg.v`.
- Parameterized `SHIFT_REG_BIT_WIDTH` (default 16; also used with 49)
- Rotating left shift (MSB wraps to LSB)
- Inputs: `clk`, `rst_n`, `step`, `set`
- Output: `shift_reg_f [SHIFT_REG_BIT_WIDTH-1:0]`

### uart_serializer

Found in `piton/design/common/uart_pkttrace_dump/rtl/uart_serializer.v`.
Look at the testbench `piton/verif/env/uart_serializer/uart_serializer_top.v`
for the exact port list. The module serializes incoming parallel data into a
UART byte stream.

